('P', 'Threshold expressions such as ">=20%=+7 | 15-19%=+5" break into many short tokens, because digits, percent signs, operators and separators tend to be tokenized individually. As a result the estimator undercounts the compressed rubric by 34.2% and the full rubric by 15.9%, while it overcounts plain-language prompts such as Thesis Tester by 14.9%. Unicode decoration is not the cause: it accounts for only 118 of the 3,645 tokens in the full prompt, and converting it to ASCII saves 26 tokens (0.7%). In practice, a quota guard built on the heuristic would admit the compressed prompt believing it costs 1,034 tokens when it actually costs 1,571.'),
