('H1', '7. Iterations, Repeated Testing and Statistical Validity'),
('P', 'A DV Score produced by a single run is a sample, not a measurement. Even a perfectly deterministic rubric converts small input errors into large output changes when an input lies near a scoring boundary. This chapter quantifies that effect.'),
('H2', '7.1 Sources of Run-to-Run Variance'),
('P', 'Two mechanisms cause a score to vary between runs. The model itself is non-deterministic even at temperature zero [6], and the retrieved inputs change, because a search may return a P/E of 24.1 from one page and 25.3 from another. The live trial P1 is designed to measure the first mechanism. Experiment E6 isolates the second by holding the scoring function fixed and perturbing only the data.'),
