('P', 'Two observations follow. Even 5% noise fails hypothesis H3: the mean SD of 2.56 points exceeds the 2-point limit, and 42.5% of companies cross a verdict band at least once in ten runs. The step-function design of the rubric is responsible; a ROE of 19.9% earns +5 whereas 20.0% earns +7. In addition, spread grows sub-linearly: the SD rises by a factor of 2.7 while noise rises by a factor of 6, because most metrics sit well inside a bucket and only those near an edge move.'),
