('P', 'The consequence is visible in Figure 9: 25% of large-caps fall into tier C, compared with 41% of mid-caps and 46% of small-caps.'),
('H2', '8.3 ESG Sensitivity (E3)'),
('P', 'Raising every G score by one point changes the tier of 105 securities (19.7%); lowering it by one point changes 143 (26.9%). Either shock changes 247 of 532 securities (46.4%, 95% CI 42.2-50.7%), so hypothesis H5 is rejected by a wide margin. The cause is structural: E and S are integers and the tier depends on their mean, so composites cluster at thirds (4.33, 5.67, 6.67) close to the cut-offs at 5.5 and 6.5.'),
